<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  mopsus — escalate a failed dispatch with a handle, every 5 minutes (plan 0046).

  A SEPARATE unit from fleet-watch on purpose (D1): the watcher is the fleet's
  dispatch thread and the one rule that keeps it debuggable is that it checks
  and moves on. Composing a brief means reading a log file and fleet.db —
  effort that belongs off that thread entirely, not deferred within it.

  Reads ~/dev/.fleet/fleet.db, which org.eunomia.fleet-collect keeps current
  on its OWN 120s cadence — this unit does not, and must not, ingest anything
  itself (docs/fleet-db.md: fleet-collect is the one writer). A host where
  fleet-collect is not installed, or has fallen behind, simply has no
  failures visible here yet; mopsus never treats that as an error.

  Install (opshost — the ledger host, alongside fleet-collect):
    mkdir -p ~/dev/.fleet
    cp launchd/org.eunomia.mopsus.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    # fill FLEET_ANGELIA_URL/APP/USER + FLEET_ANGELIA_TOKEN_CMD, or
    # FLEET_NTFY_URL, first — see below
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.mopsus.plist
  Reload after editing (a frozen job needs bootout+bootstrap, not kickstart):
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/org.eunomia.mopsus
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.mopsus.plist

  RUNS FROM THE PINNED WORKTREE, not ~/dev/eunomia — the same rule
  fleet-collect and fleet-watch's own plists state, and the same postmortem
  (ADR-0005): the shared clone sits on whatever branch a session last left it
  on, and a scheduled job is the worst place to inherit that silently.

  No page channel configured here (both env vars empty) means mopsus still
  runs, still composes briefs, still writes handles to
  ~/dev/.fleet/mopsus/briefs/ and still records every attempt in
  ~/dev/.fleet/pages.jsonl — it just prints instead of reaching a phone
  (bin/orchestrator's notify() contract, reused rather than restated here).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>org.eunomia.mopsus</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/eunomia/bin/mopsus</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <!-- angelia (preferred) -->
    <key>FLEET_ANGELIA_URL</key><string></string>
    <key>FLEET_ANGELIA_APP</key><string></string>
    <key>FLEET_ANGELIA_USER</key><string></string>
    <key>FLEET_ANGELIA_TOKEN_CMD</key><string></string>
    <!-- ntfy fallback; empty = print-only -->
    <key>FLEET_NTFY_URL</key><string></string>
  </dict>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>300</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- A read-only sweep over fleet.db and a handful of log tails; never on
       the critical path of anything a login or an active session waits on. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
  <true/>
  <key>Nice</key>
  <integer>5</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/mopsus.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/mopsus.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
